sweet-readonly-probes (lowclk 2026-11-15, goal LOWCLK-GAPS B1-B3, research docs/research/161-readonly-probes-slc-psci-wifi.md): ONE probe boot that answers three unknowns with QUERY-ONLY calls. Nothing here writes hardware; every firmware command of the batch is a read.
B1 SLC service over ACPM channel 10 (shim/sweetprobe.c + shim/acpm.c acpm_slc_describe / acpm_slc_version, build.sh --sweet-probe): the descriptors of channel 10 (slc-acpm) and 11 (its async notification channel) are READ, and ONE fixed PT_VERSION (0xd005) request goes out on channel 10 only when its descriptor validated and both queues are empty [read SG kernel/google-modules/soc/gs @ 20407875 drivers/soc/google/pt/slc_acpm.c:29-36, :126-195; research 161 s.1]. PT_CHECK (0xd003) is DROPPED: it pops a resize event and reports no enabled state [read slc_acpm.c:226-254]. PT_VERSION answers service liveness and version only: it CANNOT tell which SLC partitions are enabled (no command in the pinned source reads that, research 161 s.0, U1 stays open); a GAP line says so on every probe boot.
B2 PSCI (shim): PSCI_VERSION and PSCI_FEATURES of CPU_SUSPEND 64-bit (0xC4000001), CPU_OFF (0x84000002) and CPU_SUSPEND 32-bit (0x84000001), through a fixed id table and ONE smc in shim/sweetprobe_smc.c; CPU_SUSPEND / CPU_OFF / CPU_ON themselves are never called [read Linux v6.6 psci.h:33-50, :125-135; research 161 s.2].
B3 Wi-Fi (this patch carries the glue, the engine code is in the regenerated headers of 0201/0206): WLC_GET_PM (85), GET_VAR country, GET_VAR chanspecs, read once (P2 at the first swl25_live after L26 = "joined"; P1 "l25start", before the 4-way, is compiled but NOT armed: review 0363 finding 3, a stalled GET there would end the join; a probe GET without an answer at P2 also stops L25 and the G2 undo runs, so Wi-Fi is off for that boot, logged as `L25 STOP`: review 0363 Opus finding 1), one ioctl at a time, no retry; three new rows in the L25 store whitelist (sweet_wlan_l25_wl.h, 20 -> 23 rows; SET_PM 86, SET country and WLC_SET_COUNTRY 84 have none; the per-band chanspecs input form is refused). The Set 383 key log (sweet_wlan_sta.h swsta_p383, glue in 0201): the KEY NAME and L of every Apple80211 Set 383 call, de-duplicated (32 keys), never a value; the request is still answered "not handled".
This patch: bsd/dev/sweet_probe.c (boot-arg sweetprobe: absent / 0 = everything off, 1 = on, any other value a GAP and off; prints the shim tokens sweetprobe_pv/pf1/pf2/pf3/c10a/c10b/c11a/c11b/slcrc/slcv/slce/slcs as `SWEET PROBE:` lines with a GAP per failure, refusal, unsupported reply and missing token), the call from SweetCPU.cpp next to the --mif-clk print (patch 0214), and the glue in sweet_wlan.c that arms the Wi-Fi round (P2 only) (swl25_probe_set). Rule 8: the new hardware-facing code is the shim PT_VERSION request (acpm.c xfer_eb with 32-byte element support) and the three whitelist rows; the Opus review of them: docs/reviews/0363-probes-review-opus.md (super repo), SAFE WITH CONDITIONS, findings 1-3 fixed in 2d1e8325.
Host tests: shim/sweetprobe_host_test.c (fake 16/32 B SLC APM + fake PSCI), shim/wlan_l25_wl_host_test.c, wlan_l25_host_pr.h, wlan_sta_host_test.c; tools/sweetprobe_audit.py (source + object audit, 30 mutants), tools/test_sweetprobe_wifi_mutants.py. Not run on hardware. Boot plan: standard root, kernel with this patch, image built with tools/build-xnu-image.sh --sweet-probe (adds sweetprobe=1), grep `SWEET PROBE:`.
